<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xml:lang="en" xml:base="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/rss/news-feed/" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title type="text">News feed</title><subtitle type="text">Finanstilsynet's news feed.</subtitle><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no</id><updated>2026-07-15T11:04:05+02:00</updated><link rel="self" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/rss/news-feed/" /><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-and-vulnerability-analysis-2026/</id><title type="text">Risk and Vulnerability Analysis 2026</title><summary type="text">The report is now available in English.</summary><published>2026-07-15T11:04:05+02:00</published><updated>2026-07-15T11:04:05+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-and-vulnerability-analysis-2026/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-and-vulnerability-analysis-2026/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-outlook--june-2026---full-report/</id><title type="text">Risk Outlook – June 2026 - full report</title><summary type="text">The full report is now available in English. Please note that the cut-off date was 10 June 2026.</summary><published>2026-07-10T13:06:55+02:00</published><updated>2026-07-10T13:06:55+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-outlook--june-2026---full-report/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-outlook--june-2026---full-report/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/the-european-systemic-risk-board-esrb-warns-against-frontier-ai-models/</id><title type="text">The European Systemic Risk Board (ESRB) warns against frontier AI models</title><summary type="text">The ESRB warns that frontier AI models have increased systemic risks and challenge the resilience of the financial system. Norges Bank and Finanstilsynet support the warning.</summary><published>2026-07-07T12:01:21+02:00</published><updated>2026-07-07T12:02:09+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/the-european-systemic-risk-board-esrb-warns-against-frontier-ai-models/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/the-european-systemic-risk-board-esrb-warns-against-frontier-ai-models/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-outlook--june-2026/</id><title type="text">Risk Outlook – June 2026</title><summary type="text">Geopolitical tensions and war increase the risk of financial instability. The cyberthreat level is high, and incidents could have systemic consequences. High household debt and elevated property prices are the key vulnerabilities in the Norwegian financial system. Risk remains high within property development.</summary><published>2026-06-11T08:00:41+02:00</published><updated>2026-06-11T08:00:41+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-outlook--june-2026/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/risk-outlook--june-2026/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/invoice-for-supervisory-levy-in-2025/</id><title type="text">Invoice for supervisory levy in 2026</title><summary type="text">Finanstilsynet&amp;rsquo;s expenditure is apportioned on entities under supervision. The Norwegian Tax Administration, represented by the Norwegian National Collection Agency, sends out invoices for the supervisory levy on behalf of Finanstilsynet.</summary><published>2026-06-10T11:50:00+02:00</published><updated>2026-06-10T11:50:00+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/invoice-for-supervisory-levy-in-2025/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/invoice-for-supervisory-levy-in-2025/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/finanstilsynets-annual-report-for-2025/</id><title type="text">Finanstilsynet’s annual report for 2025</title><summary type="text">The annual report presents key tasks and initiatives carried out by Finanstilsynet in 2025. Finanstilsynet largely carried out its tasks in line with the mandate in the Ministry of Finance's letter of allocation and the adopted strategy.</summary><published>2026-05-15T13:40:25+02:00</published><updated>2026-05-15T13:40:25+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/finanstilsynets-annual-report-for-2025/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/finanstilsynets-annual-report-for-2025/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/warning-about-the-misuse-of-finanstilsynets-name/</id><title type="text">Warning about the misuse of Finanstilsynet’s name</title><summary type="text">Finanstilsynet has recently become aware of several cases of fraud in which Finanstilsynet&amp;rsquo;s name and the names of employees have been misused in connection with alleged loan transactions between group companies. So far, this has applied to transactions between Norwegian companies and their foreign subsidiaries.</summary><published>2026-05-08T15:31:03+02:00</published><updated>2026-05-08T15:31:03+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/warning-about-the-misuse-of-finanstilsynets-name/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/warning-about-the-misuse-of-finanstilsynets-name/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/finanstilsynets-priorities-for-2026/</id><title type="text">Finanstilsynet’s priorities for 2026</title><summary type="text">Finanstilsynet will promote financial stability and well-functioning markets. Six main goals have been establish to support our social mission. The follow-up of approximately 9 000 entities and 18 000 individuals under supervision will be risk-based and efficient.</summary><published>2026-04-21T08:55:18+02:00</published><updated>2026-04-21T08:55:18+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/finanstilsynets-priorities-for-2026/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/finanstilsynets-priorities-for-2026/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/reporting-from-entities-subject-to-financial-reporting-oversight-krt-1003/</id><title type="text">Reporting from entities subject to financial reporting oversight (KRT-1003)</title><summary type="text">The KRT-1003 form shall be completed by entities listed on the Oslo Stock Exchange (Oslo B&amp;oslash;rs/Euronext Expand) that issue shares, and bonds with a nominal value of less than 100 000 euro or equivalent amount in another currency, that have Norway as their home state, and that are listed at 31 December 2025.</summary><published>2026-02-25T10:05:34+01:00</published><updated>2026-02-25T10:05:34+01:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/reporting-from-entities-subject-to-financial-reporting-oversight-krt-1003/" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/reporting-from-entities-subject-to-financial-reporting-oversight-krt-1003/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/ifsca-and-finanstilsynet-sign-a-memorandum-of-understanding-mou/</id><title type="text">IFSCA and Finanstilsynet sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU)</title><summary type="text">The International Financial Services Centres Authority of India (&amp;lsquo;IFSCA&amp;rsquo;) and Finanstilsynet, the Financial Supervisory Authority of Norway, have entered into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to formalize regulatory cooperation in identified areas of mutual interest.</summary><published>2026-02-13T13:55:39+01:00</published><updated>2026-02-13T13:55:39+01:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/ifsca-and-finanstilsynet-sign-a-memorandum-of-understanding-mou/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/ifsca-and-finanstilsynet-sign-a-memorandum-of-understanding-mou/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/reports-on-finanstilsynets-supervisory-activities-in-2025/</id><title type="text">Reports on Finanstilsynet's supervisory activities in 2025</title><summary type="text">The reports present the activities carried out, including inspections, analyses and reports, licensing matters and regulatory development.</summary><published>2026-02-12T11:55:36+01:00</published><updated>2026-02-12T11:55:36+01:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/reports-on-finanstilsynets-supervisory-activities-in-2025/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2026/reports-on-finanstilsynets-supervisory-activities-in-2025/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/mandatory-xml-format-to-be-introduced-for-annex-iv-reporting-from-30-june-2026/</id><title type="text">Mandatory xml format to be introduced for Annex IV reporting from 30 June 2026</title><summary type="text">Finanstilsynet hereby announces an important change in the reporting format for Annex IV reporting under the AIF Act and AIFMD (Directive 2011/61/EU on the regulation of alternative investment fund managers).</summary><published>2025-12-12T10:30:21+01:00</published><updated>2025-12-12T10:30:21+01:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/mandatory-xml-format-to-be-introduced-for-annex-iv-reporting-from-30-june-2026/" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/mandatory-xml-format-to-be-introduced-for-annex-iv-reporting-from-30-june-2026/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--december-2025/</id><title type="text">Risk Outlook – December 2025</title><summary type="text">High household debt and elevated residential and commercial property prices remain the key vulnerabilities in the Norwegian financial system. The risk within property development is deemed to have increased. Geopolitical tensions and increased trade barriers cause considerable uncertainty about future developments.</summary><published>2025-12-04T08:15:27+01:00</published><updated>2025-12-04T08:15:27+01:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--december-2025/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--december-2025/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/cessation-of-fees-for-fund-marketing-notifications/</id><title type="text">Cessation of fees for fund marketing notifications</title><summary type="text">As of 1 October 2025, Finanstilsynet will no longer charge a registration fee or an annual fee for funds notified for marketing in Norway under the EEA passporting regime (AIFMD art. 32 and UCITS Directive art. 93). This change applies to notifications received after 30 September 2025 and covers UCITS, AIF, EuSEF, EuVECA and ELTIF funds.</summary><published>2025-10-01T10:35:02+02:00</published><updated>2025-10-01T10:35:02+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/cessation-of-fees-for-fund-marketing-notifications/" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Securities market" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/cessation-of-fees-for-fund-marketing-notifications/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--june-2025---full-report/</id><title type="text">Risk Outlook – June 2025 - full report</title><summary type="text">The full report is now available in English. Please note that the cut-off date was 4 June 2025.</summary><published>2025-07-04T16:33:44+02:00</published><updated>2025-07-04T16:33:44+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--june-2025---full-report/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--june-2025---full-report/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--june-2025/</id><title type="text">Risk Outlook – June 2025</title><summary type="text">Overall, the Norwegian economy has fared well through the inflation and interest rate shock in the wake of Russia's invasion of Ukraine. Economic growth has been moderate over the past two years, and unemployment has increased from a low level. The household debt burden has decreased somewhat but is still at a high level. Geopolitical shifts are contributing to a high degree of uncertainty regarding future developments, and the risk of global financial instability has increased.</summary><published>2025-06-05T08:02:53+02:00</published><updated>2025-07-04T16:35:13+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--june-2025/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/risk-outlook--june-2025/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/invoice-for-supervisory-levy-in-2025/</id><title type="text">Invoice for supervisory levy in 2025</title><summary type="text">Finanstilsynet&amp;rsquo;s expenditure is apportioned on entities under supervision. The Norwegian Tax Administration, represented by the Norwegian National Collection Agency, sends out invoices for the supervisory levy on behalf of Finanstilsynet. Invoices to state authorised accountants will be sent on 2 May 2025, and invoices to other categories of supervised entities will be sent in the course of week 19.</summary><published>2025-04-30T16:06:55+02:00</published><updated>2025-04-30T16:10:47+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/invoice-for-supervisory-levy-in-2025/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/invoice-for-supervisory-levy-in-2025/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/new-act-on-finanstilsynet-entered-into-force-on-1-april-2025/</id><title type="text">New Act on Finanstilsynet entered into force on 1 April 2025</title><summary type="text">The new Act on Finanstilsynet (Financial Supervision Act) replaced the previous Act on the Supervision of Financial Institutions etc. from 1956. According to the new Act, the Director General has overarching responsibility for Finanstilsynet&amp;rsquo;s operations. A new Board of Directors considers and decides individual supervisory and licensing matters.</summary><published>2025-04-08T12:01:08+02:00</published><updated>2025-04-08T12:01:08+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/new-act-on-finanstilsynet-entered-into-force-on-1-april-2025/" /><category term="Bank" /><category term="Payment institution" /><category term="Account information service provider" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Financial benchmarks" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><category term="Auditing" /><category term="External accounting" /><category term="Estate agents" /><category term="Debt collection" /><category term="Debt registry" /><category term="Company service providers" /><category term="Virtual asset service providers" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/new-act-on-finanstilsynet-entered-into-force-on-1-april-2025/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/finanstilsynet-has-taken-over-supervision-of-the-ongoing-disclosure-obligation-and-delayed/</id><title type="text">Finanstilsynet has taken over supervision of the ongoing disclosure obligation and delayed disclosure of inside information and the responsibility as takeover supervisory authority</title><summary type="text">Supervision of the rules on the ongoing disclosure obligation and delayed disclosure of inside information, supervision of share buy-backs and stabilisation, as well as the responsibility as takeover supervisory authority, have been transferred from Oslo B&amp;oslash;rs to Finanstilsynet. The transfer has been completed with effect from 1 April 2025. Finanstilsynet has updated its website with additional information on relevant regulations and practical information on the submission of Notifications of delayed disclosure via Altinn.</summary><published>2025-04-01T08:32:53+02:00</published><updated>2025-04-01T08:32:53+02:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/finanstilsynet-has-taken-over-supervision-of-the-ongoing-disclosure-obligation-and-delayed/" /><category term="Alternative investment fund manager (AIFM)" /><category term="Market conduct" /><category term="Securities market" /><category term="Prospectuses" /><category term="Financial reporting" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/finanstilsynet-has-taken-over-supervision-of-the-ongoing-disclosure-obligation-and-delayed/" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/the-financial-supervisory-authority-warns-against-insurance-and-insurance-brokerage-services-from/</id><title type="text">Finanstilsynet warns against insurance and insurance brokerage services from Romarine AS</title><summary type="text">Finanstilsynet has been informed that the company Romarine AS offers insurance and insurance brokerage services without having a license or being registered in Finanstilsynet's registry. Such activity is illegal.</summary><published>2025-03-25T15:58:59+01:00</published><updated>2025-03-25T20:44:36+01:00</updated><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/the-financial-supervisory-authority-warns-against-insurance-and-insurance-brokerage-services-from/" /><category term="Insurance and pensions" /><content type="text/html" src="https://www.finanstilsynet.no/en/news-archive/news/2025/the-financial-supervisory-authority-warns-against-insurance-and-insurance-brokerage-services-from/" /></entry></feed>